    "max_awards": null,
    "plot": "Master Artificer Corvus has vanished from his sealed workshop hours before the Guild's inspection deadline. Guild Investigator Kaelen Voss arrives to find the facility locked down, infested with haywire clockwork pests, and guarded by an aggressive security drone. Kaelen must scavenge the workshop to repair his broken Guild transmitter, forge a balanced tool, unlock the Overseer's personal safe by solving the workshop's structural riddle, and assemble the Calibrated Prototype Core. Upon powering the Prototype Station in the inner chamber, Kaelen discovers Corvus's hidden message: he faked his disappearance to keep the Guild from weaponizing his creation.",
    "rules": "Explore the four workshop rooms, combine components to craft upgraded tools and mission-critical devices, and use environmental clues to solve lock combinations. Combat uses turn-based special actions.\n\nThe Tiny Brass Key begins clamped inside Drill-Rat Alpha (HAYWIRE_DRILL_RAT_1). Its initial appearance in Kaelen's inventory represents only his Guild requisition record, not possession of the key. Until Kaelen defeats Drill-Rat Alpha and explicitly recovers the key, TINY_BRASS_KEY cannot be used, given away, or counted toward Chapter 1's item requirement, and it cannot unlock the Overseer's Office. Recovering it after that victory converts the existing inventory record into possession of the actual key; do not award a duplicate.",
    "intro_text": "The heavy iron entry hatch slams shut behind you, sealing you inside Master Corvus's Central Workbench hall. The air smells sharply of ozone, scorched machine oil, and cold brass. Across the room, the Master's famous workbenches stand cluttered with half-assembled mechanisms and spilled rivets, while three tall copper coils hum faintly along the north wall.\n\nYour Guild-issue transmitter crackles uselessly in your pocket, its antenna snapped during your descent into the facility. Before the Guild's deadline expires, you must restore communications, search the workshop for the missing components of Corvus's prototype, and discover why the Master abandoned his life's work.",
    "completed_condition": "",
